@startuml proximity-detection
title US-05: Proximity Detection - Correlation Worker uses H3 geo-cells; proximity episode model

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:{cell_id}\n(sorted set)" as GeoCell
database "Redis\nproximity-episode:{pair_key}\n(hash)" as Episode
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Alerts
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Kafka -> Correlation : consume position event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

note over Correlation
  Compute H3 cell at LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION (resolution 7 ≈ 5 km²).
  k-ring radius = ceil(PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES / cell_edge_length_at_resolution).
  Expands to all cells within proximity range.
end note

Correlation -> GeoCell : ZADD geo-cell:{live_cell_id} $now_ms $entity_id
note over GeoCell
  Score = last_seen_ms for this entity in this cell.
  Sorted set per H3 cell at LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION.
end note

Correlation -> GeoCell : ZRANGEBYSCORE geo-cell:{neighbour_cell}\n(now_ms - LIVE_PROXIMITY_MAX_AGE_MS) now_ms\n(for each cell in k-ring)
GeoCell --> Correlation : candidate entity IDs (scored by last_seen_ms)

Correlation -> Correlation : for each candidate:\nfetch entity:live:{id} from Redis\nrecheck last_seen_ms against LIVE_PROXIMITY_MAX_AGE_MS\ncompute Haversine distance

alt distance <= PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES and candidate is fresh
  Correlation -> Neo4j : MATCH (a:Entity {id: $id_a})-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(b:Entity {id: $id_b})\nRETURN b

  note over Neo4j
    Graph absence query.
    Checks for a KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge.
    Single traversal - not a table scan.
  end note

  alt no KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge found
    note over Correlation
      pair_key = min(entity_a_id, entity_b_id) + ':' + max(entity_a_id, entity_b_id)
      Canonical ordering prevents A:B and B:A being treated as different pairs.
    end note

    Correlation -> Episode : HGET proximity-episode:{pair_key} episode_start_ms
    Episode --> Correlation : nil or $episode_start_ms

    alt episode key absent (new episode)
      Correlation -> Episode : HSET proximity-episode:{pair_key}\n{ episode_start_ms: $now_ms, last_seen_ms: $now_ms }\nEXPIRE PROXIMITY_EPISODE_GAP_MS
      Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\nidempotency_key = {pair_key}:{episode_start_ms}\n(see graph-update diagram)
      Correlation -> ProxKafka : publish proximity.candidates (episode start)\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, timestamp_ms,\n  lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

      note over ProxKafka
        One proximity.candidates event per episode, not per ping.
        Alert Evaluator triggered once per encounter.
        TTL refresh (below) keeps the episode alive while pair stays close.
      end note

    else episode key exists (continuing episode)
      Correlation -> Episode : HSET proximity-episode:{pair_key} last_seen_ms $now_ms\nEXPIRE PROXIMITY_EPISODE_GAP_MS
      note over Correlation
        TTL refreshed. Episode continues.
        No new proximity.candidates published.
        Neo4j edge may be updated (last_seen_ms, min_distance_metres)
        but no new edge created.
      end note
    end

  else prior KNOWN_ASSOCIATE relationship exists
    Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge (durable record only)
    note over Correlation
      Known associate — routine proximity.
      Neo4j edge written for history.
      No proximity.candidates event published.
    end note
  end
end

== Alert Evaluator - consumes proximity.candidates ==

note over Evaluator
  Completely separate from the Correlation Worker.
  Consumes proximity.candidates events driven by Kafka.
  One event per episode — not one per ping.
  Known associates already filtered upstream.
end note

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, timestamp_ms,\n  lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

Evaluator -> Alerts : publish to alerts\n{ alert_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  entity_a, entity_b, pair_key, episode_start_ms,\n  location, distance_at_detection, timestamp_ms }

Alerts -> API : consume alert
API -> TSDB : INSERT INTO alerts\n( alert_id, entity_id, alert_type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  status: NEW, detected_at, payload )\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Idempotent write - safe under Kafka replay.
  alert_id = {pair_key}:UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY:{episode_start_ms}
end note

note over API
  Scope filter applied per connection:
  event position + entity type must match
  the operator's saved workspace scope.
end note

API --> Dashboard : push alert over WebSocket\n(scope-matched connections only)
Dashboard --> Operator : proximity alert displayed\nstatus: NEW

@enduml
